legal power to direct management and policies.

"Service Provider" means a contractor, consultant, cloud provider, hosting
provider, CI/CD provider, security reviewer, or other third party acting solely
on behalf of Your Company and only for Your Company's Permitted Internal Use.

"Permitted Internal Use" means use of the Licensed Work solely for the internal
business operations of Your Company. Permitted Internal Use includes internal
development, internal testing, internal CI/CD, internal QA, internal validation,
internal benchmarking, internal proof-of-concept work, internal security review,
internal compliance review, internal staging, and internal production use.

For clarity, Permitted Internal Use includes using the Licensed Work internally
to test, validate, simulate, benchmark, or improve software, systems, services,
or products that Your Company develops, operates, sells, or makes available to
third parties, provided that the Licensed Work itself is not distributed,
embedded, exposed, hosted, provided, or made available to those third parties.

"External Offering" means any product, service, platform, hosted service,
managed service, SaaS offering, API, appliance, marketplace offering,
consulting deliverable, outsourced operation, certification service, testing
service, simulation service, validation service, QA service, CI/CD service, or
similar offering made available to a third party.

"Commercial Redistribution" means selling, renting, leasing, sublicensing,
publishing, distributing, making available, or otherwise providing the Licensed
Work, in source or object form, to any third party, whether for payment or other
commercial advantage.

"Product Embedding" means including, bundling, embedding, integrating, linking,
packaging, containerizing, or shipping the Licensed Work as part of any product,
service, platform, appliance, SDK, developer tool, CI/CD tool, testing tool,
simulation tool, validation tool, QA platform, certification platform, or other
offering made available to a third party.

"Protected Testing Functionality" means functionality of the Licensed Work for
defining, generating, compiling, orchestrating, executing, recording,
replaying, validating, verifying, benchmarking, simulating, or reporting on
software tests, integration tests, system tests, acceptance tests, scenario
tests, probes, assertions, fixtures, generated test workspaces, generated test
