"Implementation Materials" means source code, object code, architecture,
internal APIs, command-line interfaces, configuration formats, generated
templates, test fixtures, examples, documentation, build files, scripts,
container files, scenario definitions, assertion definitions, probe
definitions, report formats, evidence formats, and other materials copied from,
adapted from, or derived from the Licensed Work.

"AI System" means any machine learning system, foundation model, large language
model, code generation model, embedding model, classifier, recommender,
automated software engineering system, agentic system, or other system that
learns from, is trained on, is fine-tuned on, is evaluated on, or generates
outputs using data or examples.

"AI Training Use" means using the Licensed Work, or any source code,
documentation, examples, tests, fixtures, configuration files, generated
templates, repository history, issues, discussions, pull requests, comments,
metadata, or other materials associated with the Licensed Work, for any of the
following purposes:

(a) training, pre-training, fine-tuning, retraining, distilling, adapting, or
    improving an AI System;

(b) creating, augmenting, cleaning, labeling, curating, validating, testing, or
    benchmarking a dataset for an AI System;

(c) evaluating, ranking, scoring, red-teaming, reinforcement-learning,
    preference-training, or otherwise improving an AI System;

(d) generating synthetic training data, code examples, documentation examples,
    test cases, fixtures, or benchmarks for an AI System;

(e) extracting, encoding, indexing, or embedding the Licensed Work for a system
    intended to reproduce, generate, explain, summarize, transform, translate,
    complete, or substitute for the Licensed Work or substantially similar
    software; or

(f) enabling a third-party AI System to retain, memorize, reproduce, generate,
    or make available source code, documentation, tests, fixtures, examples, or
    functionality derived from the Licensed Work.

"Your Materials" means software, configuration, tests, data, documentation, and
other materials created independently by You and not copied or derived from the
Licensed Work.

"Output" means a report, log, artifact, test result, generated file, simulation
result, validation result, or other output produced by running the Licensed Work
on Your Materials.

