6. Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, and Text-and-Data Mining

Licensor does not grant permission for AI Training Use.

You may not use, copy, scrape, crawl, ingest, mine, extract, process, encode,
index, embed, transform, or otherwise exploit the Licensed Work for AI Training
Use without a separate written license from Licensor.

You may not provide the Licensed Work to any third-party AI System, AI training
provider, dataset provider, model provider, code-generation provider, or similar
service if the provider may use the Licensed Work for AI Training Use, retain
the Licensed Work for model improvement, include the Licensed Work in training
or evaluation datasets, or make the Licensed Work available to other customers.

You may use AI-assisted developer tools for Permitted Internal Use only if all
of the following conditions are met:

(a) the Licensed Work is not used for AI Training Use;

(b) the AI-assisted tool provider is contractually or technically prohibited
    from using the Licensed Work for training, fine-tuning, evaluation, dataset
    creation, model improvement, or other AI Training Use;

(c) the Licensed Work is not retained by the AI-assisted tool provider beyond
    transient processing necessary to provide the requested assistance, except
    where retained solely under Your Company's private account, private tenant,
    or private enterprise configuration and not used for any third-party model
    training or service improvement; and

(d) the AI-assisted use does not result in publication, redistribution,
    disclosure, or third-party availability of the Licensed Work.

For purposes of Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790 on copyright and
related rights in the Digital Single Market, and any analogous text-and-data
mining, machine-learning, or AI-training exception under applicable law,
Licensor expressly reserves all rights to the Licensed Work for text and data
mining, data scraping, machine learning, AI training, AI evaluation, model
development, model improvement, dataset creation, and similar computational
analysis. This reservation applies in all formats and through all channels,
including source repositories, package registries, websites, archives, APIs,
